_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Pre-check failures should not abort `publish_inbox_relays`**

Line 260 propagates `inbox_relay_event_is_current` errors with `?`. That makes this path fail hard on transient fetch/no-relay conditions, while publish failures later are still handled as best-effort. This inconsistency can break startup behavior unexpectedly.



<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
-        if self.inbox_relay_event_is_current(&relay_urls).await? {
-            info!("Skipping kind 10050 publish; inbox relay list unchanged");
-            return Ok(());
-        }
+        match self.inbox_relay_event_is_current(&relay_urls).await {
+            Ok(true) => {
+                info!("Skipping kind 10050 publish; inbox relay list unchanged");
+                return Ok(());
+            }
+            Ok(false) => {}
+            Err(e) => {
+                warn!(
+                    error = %e,
+                    "Failed to verify existing kind 10050 event; proceeding to publish"
+                );
+            }
+        }
```
</details>


